id: pm-yjq2x0
title: Stop in-flight telemetry capture after persisted consent is cleared
description: "An invocation started while telemetry is enabled can finish after persisted telemetry is disabled or cleared. finishTelemetryCommand currently checks only process opt-outs and retains the old installation identity. Reproduce the public SDK sequence in isolated trackers, recheck persisted consent and identity before completion capture, and distinguish already-dispatched network requests from newly captured data."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-13T21:36:42.809Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-13T22:30:06.163Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-13T22:30:05.196Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-13T22:30:05.196Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A deferred failed read creates no completion artifacts after persisted disable; clear then reenable cannot reuse an old active installation identity; enabled unchanged installations retain lifecycle pairs; all-source coverage and public SDK regression tests pass
goal: project management = context management
objective: Honor persisted telemetry consent throughout an invocation lifecycle
value: Privacy-safe operational context for long-running SDK and CLI consumers
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: Recheck saved consent and installation identity before deferred start and completion capture
expected_result: "An invocation finishing after disable, clear, or clear then reenable does not recreate events under revoked consent or identity"
actual_result: All three negative controls and packed npm/Bun public SDK acceptance pass; full 8832-test regression has exact 100/100/100/100 coverage
component: telemetry completion capture
